      "extract": "What is now called Gröbner and Gröbner-Shirshov bases theory was initiated by A. I. Shirshov (1921-1981) [@Sh62a; @Sh62b], 1962 for non-associative and Lie algebras, by H. Hironaka [@Hi64; @{Hi64-}], 1964 for quotients of commutative infinite series algebras (both formal and convergent), and by B. Buchberger [@bu65; @bu70], 1965, 1970 for commutative algebras. English translation of selected works of A. I. Shirshov,",
